section.para:
Python's operators, applied to the Python object and the argument (or
to the object alone, for the prefix operators):
+, -, *,
/, ** are Python's;
%, Rexx's integer division, is Python's //;
//, Rexx's remainder, is Python's %;
the prefix \ is Python's not.
The result follows : a Python number
comes back as a Rexx string, a numpy array as a
PyObject. See .

listitem.para:
o~name calls it with no
arguments when it is a function or a method, and returns it otherwise
(classes and modules are returned);

section.para:
Returns the item at position, from 1;
&nil; outside 1 to items. The position must be a
whole number.
